he correct answer.\n</think>\n\nTo determine how deep the river is by mid-July, follow these steps:\n\n1. **Mid-May**: The river is 5 feet deep.\n2. **Mid-June**: The river is 10 feet deeper than mid-May, so:\n   $$\n   \\text{Deeper by mid-June} = 5 + 10 = 15 \\, \\text{feet}\n   $$\n3. **Mid-July**: The river is three times as deep as mid-June, so:\n   $$\n   \\text{Depth by mid-July} = 15 \\times 3 = 45 \\, \\text{feet}\n   $$\n\n**Final Answer**: $\\boxed{45}$ feet deep is the river by mid-July.<|im_end|>", "source_record": {"question": "In mid-May, the river flowing through Moreland is five feet deep. By mid-June, the river is 10 feet deeper than mid-May. By mid-July, the river is three times deeper than mid-June. How many feet deep is the river by mid-July?", "answer": "In mid-June, the river is 5+10=<<5+10=15>>15 feet deep.\nIn mid-July, the river is 15*3=<<15*3=45>>45 feet deep.\n#### 45", "prompt": "Solve the following grade-school math problem. Show your reasoning and put the final answer in \\boxed{}.\n\nProblem: In mid-May, the river flowing through Moreland is five feet deep. By mid-June, the river is 10 feet deeper than mid-May. By mid-July, the river is three times deeper than mid-June. How many feet deep is the river by mid-July?\nSolution:", "solutions": ["45"], "solution": "45"}, "prompt_tokens": [151644, 872, 198, 50, 3948, 279, 2701, 11972, 34689, 6888, 3491, 13, 6928, 697, 32711, 323, 2182, 279, 1590, 4226, 304, 1124, 79075, 6257, 382, 31198, 25, 758, 5099, 61986, 11, 279, 14796, 35512, 1526, 4398, 1933, 374, 4236, 7541, 5538, 13, 3216, 5099, 12009, 2886, 11, 279, 14796, 374, 220, 16, 15, 7541, 19117, 1091, 5099, 61986, 13, 3216, 5099, 12009, 3901, 11], "response_tokens": [151667, 198, 32313, 11, 1077, 594, 1490, 13, 576, 3491, 374, 911, 9271, 279, 7990, 315, 279, 14796, 553, 5099, 12009, 3901, 13, 6771, 752, 1191, 553, 14719, 1495, 279, 1995, 2661, 382, 5338, 11, 5099, 61986, 374, 4236, 7541, 5538, 13, 5005, 553, 5099, 12009, 2886, 11, 279, 147