s total earnings after 3 years\". So if the first year is 12 months, and then the next two years are also 12 months, then total earnings would be 12 * (7,800 + 10,140 + 13,182) ?\n\nWait, no, that would be if each year's salary is calculated monthly. But if each year's salary is s, then over 3 years, it's 12 * s1 + 12 * s2 + 12 * s3? Or is it s1 + s2 + s3 where each is per month?\n\nWait, let me clarify. Let me think about earning.\n\nEarnings are his salary per month multiplied by the number of months worked. So first, starting month is 1st month, so after 1 year (12 months), his salary is 7,800/month. Then, if he works another 12 months, second year, so total 24 months, earning is 12 * 7,800 + 12 * 10,140 + 12 * 13,182.\n\nBut the problem says \"after a year of working, his salary increased by 30%. How much are his total earnings after 3 years?\"\n\nSo perhaps the problem is expecting that after a year of working (so starting at month 1, and after 12 months), his salary increased by 30%. Therefore, for the first year (months 1-12), he earns 12 * 7,800. Then for the next year (months 13-24), his salary is increased by 30%, so 12 * 10,140. Then the third year (months 25-36) would be 12 * 13,182. Therefore total earnings would be 12*(7,800 + 10,140 + 13,182).\n\nBut maybe the problem is intended to consider that after the first year, he has 30% more, and that is the only increase, but he works 3 years, so that would be 3 years of salary. However, if there is a 30% increase after each year, then each year's salary is 1.3 times the previous year's. So total earnings would be sum of each year's salary multiplied by 12 months? Or multiplied by the number of months?\n\nWait, perhaps the problem is simpler. Let me think differently. Maybe it's not about increasing the salary each year, but just increasing the salary by 30% at the end of the year. So if he ends up with a salary after one year, then after another year, and so on. But then how much is his total earnings?\n\nAlternatively, perhaps the problem is looking for the amount that would be his earnings after three years, considering the increases?\n\nWait, but let me think. If he starts", "source_record": {"question": "Kirt has a $6000 monthly salary when he started his job. After a year of working, his salary increased by 30%. How much are his total earnings after 3 years?", "answer": "His annual salary for the first year of working is 6000 x 12= $<<6000*12=72000>>72000.\nKirt's monthly increase is $6000 x 30/100= $<<6000*30/100=1800>>1800.\nSo, he received $6000 + $1800= $<<6000+1800=7800>>7800 monthly on the second and third year of working.\nKirt's annual salary in the second and third year was $7800 x 12 = $93600.\n\nThus, his total earning after 3 years is $72000 + $93600 + $93600 = $<<72000+93600+93600=259200>>259200.\n#### 259200", "prompt": "Solve the following grade-school math problem. Show your reasoning and put the final answer in \\boxed{}.\n\nProblem: Kirt has a $6000 monthly salary when he started his job. After a year of working, his salary increased by 30%. How much are his total earnings after 3 years?\nSolution:", "solutions": ["259200"], "solution": "259200"}, "prompt_tokens": [151644, 872, 198, 50, 3948, 279, 2701, 11972, 34689, 6888, 3491, 13, 6928, 697, 32711, 323, 2182, 279, 1590, 4226, 304, 1124, 79075, 6257, 382, 31198, 25, 730, 2106, 702, 264, 400, 21, 15, 15, 15, 15088, 16107, 979, 566, 3855, 806, 2618, 13, 4636, 264, 1042, 315, 3238, 11, 806, 16107, 7172, 553, 220, 18, 15, 14360, 2585, 1753, 525, 806, 2790, 23681], "response_tokens": [151667, 198, 32313, 11, 773, 730, 2106, 8471, 448, 264, 15088, 16107, 315, 400, 21, 11, 15, 15, 15, 518, 4231, 220, 17, 15, 304, 806, 2618, 13, 4636, 264, 1042, 315, 3238, 11, 806, 16107, 12703, 553, 220, 18, 15, 14360, 5005, 11, 582, 1184, 311, 7071, 700, 806, 2790, 23681, 1283, 220, 18, 1635, 13, 6771, 752, 1438, 419, 1495, 3019, 553]}
