 should be 16 - 3 = 13. Let me verify once more. \n\nYes, 28 minus 12 is 16, then 16 minus 3 is 13. So, the answer should be 13 ceilings left to paint. Let me make sure I didn't make any mistakes here. Alternatively, maybe I can approach it using fractions to avoid decimal calculations.\n\nSo, total ceilings: 28. Painted this week: 12. Painted next week: 1/4 * 12 = 3. Therefore, painted total so far: 12 + 3 = 15. Therefore, remaining ceilings: 28 - 15 = 13. Yep, same answer. \n\nI think that's correct. So, the final answer is 13.\n</think>\n\nMichelangelo starts with 28 ceilings to paint. This week, he paints 12, leaving him with $28 - 12 = 16$ ceilings to paint.\n\nNext week, he paints $\\frac{1}{4}$ of the 12 ceilings he previously painted, which is $\\frac{12}{4} = 3$. Therefore, after this week and next week, he paints 12 (this week) + 3 (next week) = 15 ceilings.\n\nFinally, the number of ceilings remaining to paint is $28 - 15 = \\boxed{13}$.<|im_end|>", "source_record": {"question": "Michelangelo has 28 ceilings to paint. This week, he paints 12 of them. Next week, he will paint 1/4 the number of ceilings he did this week. How many ceilings will be left to paint after next week?", "answer": "After this week, Michelangelo will have 28-12=<<28-12=16>>16 more ceilings to paint.\nNext week, Michelangelo will paint 12/4=<<12/4=3>>3 ceilings.\nMichelangelo will have 16-3=<<16-3=13>>13 more ceilings to paint.\n#### 13", "prompt": "Solve the following grade-school math problem. Show your reasoning and put the final answer in \\boxed{}.\n\nProblem: Michelangelo has 28 ceilings to paint. This week, he paints 12 of them. Next week, he will paint 1/4 the number of ceilings he did this week. How many ceilings will be left to paint after next week?\nSolution:", "solutions": ["13"], "solution": "13"}, "prompt_tokens": [151644, 872, 198, 50, 3948, 279, 2701, 11972, 34689, 6888, 3491, 13, 6928, 697, 32711, 323, 2182, 279, 1590, 4226, 304, 1124, 79075, 6257, 382, 31198, 25, 44