 solve the problem, let’s define the number of male members as $ x $. According to the information given, there are **two times as many female members** as male members. So, the number of female members is $ 2x $. \n\nThe total number of members in the club is 18, so we can set up the equation:\n\n$$\nx + 2x = 18\n$$\n\n$$\n3x = 18\n$$\n\n$$\nx = 6\n$$\n\nThis means there are **6 male members**. To find the number of female members, we multiply by 2:\n\n$$\n2x = 2 \\times 6 = 12\n$$\n\nThus, there are 12 female members in the glee club.\n\n$$\n\\boxed{12}\n$$<|im_end|>", "source_record": {"question": "In a glee club, there are two times as many female than male members. How many female members are there if there are 18 members in the club?", "answer": "The club has a female group which has twice as many members as the male group, so there are 2+1=<<2+1=3>>3 groups in the club.\nThere are 18 members in the club, which means there are 18/3 = <<18/3=6>>6 members per group.\nSince the number of female members consists of two groups, then there are 6 * 2 = <<6*2=12>>12 female members in the club.\n#### 12", "prompt": "Solve the following grade-school math problem. Show your reasoning and put the final answer in \\boxed{}.\n\nProblem: In a glee club, there are two times as many female than male members. How many female members are there if there are 18 members in the club?\nSolution:", "solutions": ["12"], "solution": "12"}, "prompt_tokens": [151644, 872, 198, 50, 3948, 279, 2701, 11972, 34689, 6888, 3491, 13, 6928, 697, 32711, 323, 2182, 279, 1590, 4226, 304, 1124, 79075, 6257, 382, 31198, 25, 758, 264, 342, 8501, 6335, 11, 1052, 525, 1378, 3039, 438, 1657, 8778, 1091, 8593, 3613, 13, 2585, 1657, 8778, 3613, 525, 1052, 421, 1052, 525, 220, 16, 23, 3613, 304, 279, 6335, 5267, 36842, 25, 151645], "response_tokens": [151667, 198, 32313, 11, 1077, 594, 1490, 13, 576, 3491, 2727, 1052, 525, 1378, 3039, 438, 1657, 8778, 3613, 438, 8593, 3613, 304, 264, 342, 8501, 6335, 13, 159