2026-10-30 04:23:32 INFO areno.api.trainers.policy_only.PolicyOnlyTrainer policy_only.py:723 - rollout_completion={"kind": "rollout", "epoch": 0, "step": 32, "prompt_idx": 0, "sample_idx": 0, "prompt": "Solve the following grade-school math problem. Show your reasoning and put the final answer in \\boxed{}.\n\nProblem: Rafael works 10 hours on Monday and 8 hours on Tuesday on his delivery job. With 20 hours left to work in the week, how much money does Rafael make if he is paid $20 per hour?\nSolution:", "decoded_prompt": "<|im_start|>user\nSolve the following grade-school math problem. Show your reasoning and put the final answer in \\boxed{}.\n\nProblem: Rafael works 10 hours on Monday and 8 hours on Tuesday on his delivery job. With 20 hours left to work in the week, how much money does Rafael make if he is paid $20 per hour?\nSolution:<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\n", "completion": "<think>\nOkay, so Rafael works 10 hours on Monday and 8 hours on Tuesday. That adds up to 18 hours so far. The week has 20 hours left. Hmmm, need to find out how much money he makes if he's paid $20 per hour.\n\nFirst, I should add up the hours he has already worked. 10 + 8 is 18. So he has 20 - 18 = 2 hours left. Then, multiply that by $20 per hour. Let me check the math again. 2 hours times $20. That should be $40. So the answer is $40. That makes sense. Let me make sure there's no trick here. The problem says \"with 20 hours left to work in the week,\" so yeah, subtracting his already worked hours from the remaining gives 2 hours. Yep, times $20 is correct. I think that's the answer.\n</think>\n\nTo determine how much money Rafael makes, we start by calculating the total hours he has already worked:\n\n- Monday: 10 hours\n- Tuesday: 8 hours\n\nTotal hours worked:  \n$10 + 8 = 18$ hours\n\nRemaining hours:  \n$20 - 18 = 2$ hours\n\nRafael is paid $20 per hour, so the total amount he makes is:  \n$2 \\times 20 = 40$ dollars.\n\nThe final answer is $\\boxed{40}$.<|im_end|>", "source_record": {"question": "Rafael works 10 hours on Monday and 8 hours on Tuesday on his delivery job. With 20 hours left to work in the week, how much money does Rafael make if he is paid $20 per hour?", "answer": "The total number of hours that Rafael has worked by Tuesday is 8+10 = <<8+10=18>>18 hours.\nTo complete his assigned work hours, Rafael works 20 hours more, making his total weekly hours to be 18+20 = <<38=38>>38 hours.\nSince he is paid $20 per hour, he makes $20*38 = $<<20*38=760>>760 a week.\n#### 760", "prompt": "Solve the following grade-school math problem. Show your reasoning and put the final answer in \\boxed{}.\n\nProblem: Rafael works 10 hours on Monday and 8 hours on Tuesday on his delivery job. With 20 hours left to work in the week, how much money does Rafael make if he is paid $20 per hour?\nSolution:", "solutions": ["760"], "solution": "760"}, "prompt_tokens": [151644, 872, 198, 50, 3948, 279, 2701, 11972, 34689, 6888, 3491, 13, 6928, 697, 32711, 323, 2182, 279, 1590, 4226, 304, 1124, 79075, 6257, 382, 31198, 25, 54400, 4278, 220, 16, 15, 4115, 389, 7014, 323, 220, 23, 4115, 389, 7589, 389, 806, 9691, 2618, 13, 3085, 220, 17, 15, 4115, 2115, 311, 975, 304, 279, 2003, 11, 1246, 1753, 3220, 1558, 54400, 1281], "response_tokens": [151667, 198, 32313, 11, 773, 54400, 4278, 220, 16, 15, 4115, 389, 7014, 323, 220, 23, 4115, 389, 7589, 13, 2938, 11367, 705, 311, 220, 16, 23, 4115, 773, 3041, 13, 576, 2003, 702, 220, 17, 15, 4115, 2115, 13, 472, 48886, 11, 1184, 311, 1477, 700, 1246, 1753, 3220, 566, 3643, 421, 566, 594, 7171, 400, 17, 15, 817, 6460, 382, 5338, 11]}
