a is 5 inches taller than Kelly. So, Jana's height would be Kelly's height plus 5 inches. So:\n\nJana's height = Kelly's height + 5 inches\n\nSubstituting the Kelly's height we found, which is 69 inches:\n\nJana's height = 69 + 5 = 74 inches.\n\nLet me check again to make sure I didn't mix up any numbers. Starting from Jess: 72 inches. Subtract 3 inches to get Kelly: 72 - 3 = 69. Then add 5 inches: 69 + 5 = 74. No, that seems correct.\n\nWait, another way to think about it: Maybe using algebra to represent the equations. Let me try that approach too, just to confirm.\n\nLet me let J represent Jess, K represent Kelly, and Jana represent Jana. So:\n\nJess (J) = 72 inches.\n\nAccording to the problem, Kelly (K) is 3 inches shorter than Jess. So K = J - 3 inches. Which gives us K = 72 - 3 = 69 inches.\n\nThen, Jana (J) is 5 inches taller than Kelly: J = K + 5. Since K is 69, J = 69 + 5 = 74. Yep, same result. \n\nSo, that seems consistent. Therefore, Jana is 74 inches tall.\n\nWait, is there any other way that this could be interpreted? Let me check again. The problem says Jana is 5 inches taller than Kelly, and Kelly is 3 inches shorter than Jess. So, converting these into equations:\n\nJana - Kelly = 5 inches,\n\nKelly - Jess = -3 inches.\n\nBut since Jess is 72, and Kelly is 3 inches shorter than Jess, that gives Jess - Kelly = 3 inches, so Jess = Kelly + 3. Then Jana = Kelly + 5. Which again leads us to the same values.\n\nSo, no matter how I approach it, the answer seems to be 74 inches. \n\nLet me just confirm once more without breaking down step by step. If Jess is 72, then Kelly is 72 - 3 = 69. Then Jana is 69 + 5 = 74. Yep, that's straightforward. \n\nI don't see any errors in my reasoning. All the steps are logical, and the calculations seem correct. Therefore, I can be confident that Jana is 74 inches tall.\n</think>\n\nTo determine how tall Jana is, we begin by examining the relationships between their heights:\n\n- **Jess** is 72 inches tall.\n- **Kelly** is 3 inches shorter than **Jess**, so her height is $ 72 - 3 = 69 $ inches.\n- **Jana** is 5 inches taller than **Kelly**, so her height is $ 69 + 5 = 74 $ inches.\n\n### Final Answer:\n$$\n\\boxed{74}\n$$<|im_end|>", "source_record": {"question": "Jana is 5 inches taller than Kelly, and Kelly is 3 inches shorter than Jess. If Jess is 72 inches tall, how tall is Jana?", "answer": "Kelly is 72-3=<<72-3=69>>69 inches tall.\nJana is 69+5=<<69+5=74>>74 inches tall.\n#### 74", "prompt": "Solve the following grade-school math problem. Show your reasoning and put the final answer in \\boxed{}.\n\nProblem: Jana is 5 inches taller than Kelly, and Kelly is 3 inches shorter than Jess. If Jess is 72 inches tall, how tall is Jana?\nSolution:", "solutions": ["74"], "solution": "74"}, "prompt_tokens": [151644, 872, 198, 50, 3948, 279, 2701, 11972, 34689, 6888, 3491, 13, 6928, 697, 32711, 323, 2182, 279, 1590, 4226, 304, 1124, 79075, 6257, 382, 31198, 25, 619, 3362, 374, 220, 20, 14924, 49909, 1091, 18661, 11, 323, 18661, 374, 220, 18, 14924, 23327, 1091, 23039, 13, 1416, 23039, 374, 220, 22, 17, 14924, 16217, 11, 1246, 16217, 374, 619, 3362, 5267, 36842, 25], "response_tokens": [151667, 198, 32313, 11, 1077, 752, 1430, 311, 7071, 700, 419, 3491, 13, 2055, 11, 279, 3405, 374, 911, 9271, 700, 1246, 16217, 619, 3362, 374, 3118, 389, 279, 35294, 315, 3800, 13, 6771, 752, 1349, 432, 1549, 15516, 382, 41, 3362, 374, 220, 20, 14924, 49909, 1091, 18661, 11, 323, 18661, 374, 220, 18, 14924, 23327, 1091, 23039, 13, 23039, 374, 220, 22]}
