 12 is 180. No, 15 times 12 is indeed 180. So 200 minus 180 is 20. Yeah, that seems correct. So the answer is 20 unused streetlights. \n\nI don't think there's any trick here. The problem seems straightforward. Maybe the solution is just the difference between the total number of streetlights and the required number. So, 200 minus 180 equals 20. Yep, that seems right. I don't see any other steps needed here. Maybe if there were more squares or different numbers per park, the problem would be different, but as given, this seems to be the case.\n</think>\n\nTo solve the problem:\n\n1. **Determine the total number of required streetlights**:  \n   - There are 15 squares, each requiring 12 streetlights.  \n   - Total required: $ 15 \\times 12 = 180 $ streetlights.\n\n2. **Determine the number of unused streetlights**:  \n   - The city council has 200 streetlights.  \n   - Up to 180 are used, so the unused ones are:  \n     $ 200 - 180 = 20 $.\n\n---\n\n**Final Answer:**\n\n$$\n\\boxed{20}\n$$<|im_end|>", "source_record": {"question": "The New York City Council bought 200 streetlights to modernize its squares. But they don't have enough squares to use all the streetlights bought. Knowing that there are 15 squares in New York and that each park will have 12 new streetlights bought by the city council, how many unused streetlights will remain?", "answer": "So the total number of streetlights that will be used is 15 squares * 12 streetlights/square = <<15*12=180>>180 streetlights\nThere will be 200 streetlights - 180 streetlights = <<200-180=20>>20 streetlights unused.\n#### 20", "prompt": "Solve the following grade-school math problem. Show your reasoning and put the final answer in \\boxed{}.\n\nProblem: The New York City Council bought 200 streetlights to modernize its squares. But they don't have enough squares to use all the streetlights bought. Knowing that there are 15 squares in New York and that each park will have 12 new streetlights bought by the city council, how many unused streetlights will remain?\nSolution:", "solutions": ["20"], "solution": "20"}, "prompt_tokens": [151644, 872, 198, 50, 3948, 279, 2701, 11972, 34689, 6888, 3491, 13, 6928, 697, 32711, 323, 2182, 279, 1590, 4226, 304, 1124, 79075, 6257, 382, 31198, 25, 576, 1532, 4261, 4311, 9074, 10788, 220, 17, 15, 15, 8592, 13826, 311, 6481, 551, 1181, 31340, 13, 1988, 807, 1513, 944, 614, 3322, 31340, 311, 990, 678, 279, 8592, 13826, 10788, 13, 57633, 429, 1052, 525], "response_tokens": [151667, 198, 32313, 11, 1077, 752, 1430, 311, 7071, 700, 419, 3491, 13, 2055, 11, 279, 1532, 4261, 4311, 9074, 10788, 220, 17, 15, 15, 8592, 13826, 13, 2379, 614, 220, 16, 20, 31340, 11, 323, 1817, 6118, 3880, 220, 16, 17, 501, 6174, 13, 358, 1184, 311, 1477, 700, 1246, 1657, 20006, 8592, 13826, 1052, 686, 387, 382, 5338, 11, 358, 1265, 1779]}
