Rectangle: 3*6=18. Square: 5*5=25. 25-18=7. Yeah, that seems right. I don't think I made any mistakes here. Maybe visualize it: the rectangle is wider than the square, so its area is smaller, so when you subtract the square from the rectangle, it gives a positive result, which aligns with the answer 7. So I think that's the correct answer.\n</think>\n\nTo find the difference in area between the rectangle and the square:\n\n1. **Calculate the area of the rectangle**:\n   The rectangle has a length of 3 inches and a width of 6 inches. Its area is:\n   $$\n   3 \\times 6 = 18 \\text{ square inches}\n   $$\n\n2. **Calculate the area of the square**:\n   The square has a side length of 5 inches (since it's a square). Its area is:\n   $$\n   5 \\times 5 = 25 \\text{ square inches}\n   $$\n\n3. **Find the difference in areas**:\n   $$\n   25 - 18 = 7 \\text{ square inches}\n   $$\n\n**Final Answer**: $\\boxed{7}$<|im_end|>", "source_record": {"question": "A rectangle has a length of 3 inches and a width of 6 inches. A square has a width of 5 inches. What is the difference in area between the two shapes?", "answer": "The area of the rectangle is 3 x 6 = <<3*6=18>>18 sq in\nThe area of the square is 5 x 5 = <<5*5=25>>25 sq in\nThe difference is 25 - 18 = <<25-18=7>>7 sq in\n#### 7", "prompt": "Solve the following grade-school math problem. Show your reasoning and put the final answer in \\boxed{}.\n\nProblem: A rectangle has a length of 3 inches and a width of 6 inches. A square has a width of 5 inches. What is the difference in area between the two shapes?\nSolution:", "solutions": ["7"], "solution": "7"}, "prompt_tokens": [151644, 872, 198, 50, 3948, 279, 2701, 11972, 34689, 6888, 3491, 13, 6928, 697, 32711, 323, 2182, 279, 1590, 4226, 304, 1124, 79075, 6257, 382, 31198, 25, 362, 22756, 702, 264, 3084, 315, 220, 18, 14924, 323, 264, 2374, 315, 220, 21, 14924, 13, 362, 9334, 702, 264, 2374, 315, 220, 20, 14924, 13, 3555, 374, 279, 6672, 304, 3082, 1948, 279, 1378, 20816], "